<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<exercisegroup xml:id="exercise-neighborhoods" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>
    Neighborhoods
  </title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Determine whether or not the given set is a neighborhood of the given point.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  
  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Let
        
        <md>
          A = \opint{ 0 }{ 2 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \lt x \lt 2 }
        </md>
        
        be the open interval between <m> 0 </m> and <m> 2 </m>. Determine whether or not <m> A </m> is a neighborhood of the point <m> 1 </m> in the metric space <m> \of{ \R , d } </m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m> A </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 1 </m> in <m> \R </m>.
      </p>
    </answer>
    
    <solution>
      <p>
        Since <m> A </m> contains the open ball
        
        <md>
          <mrow>
            \mB_{ 1 } \of{ 1 } \amp = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ \abs{ x - 1 } \lt 1 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \lt x \lt 2 }
          </mrow>
          
          <mrow>
            \amp = \opint{ 0 }{ 2 } = A
          </mrow>
        </md>
        
        of radius <m> 1 </m> and center <m> 1 </m>, <m> A </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 1 </m> in <m> \R </m>.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Let
        
        <md>
          B = \clint{ 0 }{ 2 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \leq x \leq 2 }
        </md>
        
        be the closed interval between <m> 0 </m> and <m> 2 </m>. Determine whether or not <m> B </m> is a neighborhood of the point <m> 1 </m> in the metric space <m> \of{ \R , d } </m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m> B </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 1 </m> in <m> \R </m>.
      </p>
    </answer>
    
    <solution>
      <p>
        Since <m> B </m> contains the open ball
        
        <md>
          <mrow>
            \mB_{ 1 } \of{ 1 } \amp = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ \abs{ x - 1 } \lt 1 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \lt x \lt 2 }
          </mrow>
          
          <mrow>
            \amp = \opint{ 0 }{ 2 } \subsetneq \clint{ 0 }{ 2 } = B
          </mrow>
        </md>
        
        of radius <m> 1 </m> and center <m> 1 </m>, <m> B </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 1 </m> in <m> \R </m>.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Let
        
        <md>
          C = \clopint{ 0 }{ 2 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \leq x \lt 2 }
        </md>
        
        be the half-closed, half-open interval between <m> 0 </m> and <m> 2 </m>. Determine whether or not <m> C </m> is a neighborhood of the point <m> 0 </m> in the metric space <m> \of{ \R , d } </m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m> C </m> is not a neighborhood of <m> 0 </m> in <m> \R </m>.
      </p>
    </answer>
    
    <solution>
      <p>
        We note that for any positive real number <m> r \gt 0 </m>, the open ball
        
        <md>
          \mB_{ r } \of{ 0 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ \abs{ x - 0 } \lt r } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ -r \lt x \lt r } = \opint{ -r }{ r }
        </md>
        
        contains negative numbers. Thus any neighborhood of <m> 0 </m> in <m> \R </m> contains negative numbers. Since every element of <m> C </m> is non-negative, <m> C </m> is not a neighborhood of <m> 1 </m> in <m> \R </m>.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Let
        
        <md>
          D = 2 \Z = \setmid{ 2 k \in \Z }{ k \in \Z } = \set{ \dotsc , -6 , -4 , -2 , 0 , 2 , 4 , 6 , \dotsc }
        </md>
        
        be the set of even integers. Determine whether or not <m> D </m> is a neighborhood of the point <m> 0 </m> in the discrete metric space <m> \of{ \R , \delta_{ \R } } </m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m> D </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 0 </m> in <m> \of{ \R , \delta_{ \R } } </m>.
      </p>
    </answer>
    
    <solution>
      <p>
        We note that since the discrete metric <m> \delta_{ \R } </m> takes only the values <m> 0 </m> and <m> 1 </m>,
        
        <md>
          \mB_{ \frac{ 1 }{ 2 } } \of{ 0 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ \delta_{ \R } \of{ x , 0 } \lt \frac{ 1 }{ 2 } } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ \delta_{ \R } \of{ x , 0 } = 0 } = \set{ 0 }
        </md>.
        
        Since <m> 0 \in D </m>, <m> \mB_{ \frac{ 1 }{ 2 } } \of{ 0 } \subseteq D </m>, and so <m> D </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 0 </m> in <m> \of{ \R , \delta_{ \R } } </m>.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
  
  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Let
        
        <md>
          E = \clint{ 0 }{ 1 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \leq x \leq 1 }
        </md>
        
        be the closed interval between <m> 0 </m> and <m> 1 </m>. Determine whether or not <m> E </m> is a neighborhood of the point <m> 0 </m> in the metric subspace <m> \of{ \clint{ 0 }{ 2 } , d } </m> of the real line <m> \of{ \R , d } </m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m> E </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 0 </m> in <m> \clint{ 0 }{ 2 } </m>.
      </p>
    </answer>
    
    <solution>
      <p>
        Since <m> E </m> contains the open ball
        
        <md>
          <mrow>
            \mB_{ 1 } \of{ 0 } \amp = \setmid{ x \in \clint{ 0 }{ 2 } }{ \abs{ x - 0 } \lt 1 } = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \leq x \leq 2 \textrm{ and } -1 \lt x \lt 1 }
          </mrow>
          
          <mrow>
            \amp = \setmid{ x \in \R }{ 0 \leq x \lt 1 } = \clopint{ 0 }{ 1 } \subseteq \clint{ 0 }{ 1 } = E
          </mrow>
        </md>
        
        of radius <m> 1 </m> and center <m> 1 </m>, <m> E </m> is a neighborhood of <m> 1 </m> in <m> \clint{ 0 }{ 2 } </m>.
      </p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
</exercisegroup>
